description:
Document processing for agents

Create an extraction configuration from a JSON Schema you already have, and return its configuration id for use with `extractFile`. Supply either a `templateId` from `searchSchemaTemplates` (the server loads the schema for you) or an explicit `dataSchema` — a schema you wrote, or a template schema you edited. Unlike `generateExtractionConfig`, this needs no sample file and involves no LLM step. This tool is part of plugin `LlamaParse`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__llamaparse_createextractionconfigfromschema(args: {
  // An explicit JSON Schema object describing the fields to extract. Must be an object schema with a `properties` map. Provide this or `templateId`, not both.
  dataSchema?: { [key: string]: unknown; };
  // Whether to produce one object per document (default), per page, or per table row. Turbo supports per_doc only.
  extractionTarget?: "per_doc" | "per_page" | "per_table_row";
  // Human-readable name for the configuration. Defaults to the template title, or "extraction-config" for an explicit schema.
  name?: string;
  // Project ID that the tool should use. Uses the default project if not provided.
  projectId?: string;
  // ID of a starter template to use verbatim, as returned by `searchSchemaTemplates`. Provide this or `dataSchema`, not both.
  templateId?: string;
  // Extraction quality tier. Defaults to cost_effective (5 credits/page); agentic (15) handles complex or ambiguous documents and agentic_plus (50) is the most capable. turbo (35) is the speed tier: it returns in seconds on short documents, but it produces no parse output, accepts only PDF, JPG and PNG, and supports extractionTarget per_doc only. Turbo bills more per page than agentic — it pays for latency, not for savings, so pick it only when response time is user-facing.
  tier?: "cost_effective" | "agentic" | "agentic_plus" | "turbo";
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Document processing for agents

Extract structured data from a file based on the configuration created with the `generateExtractionConfig` tool. Returns the extracted structured data. This tool is part of plugin `LlamaParse`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__llamaparse_extractfile(args: {
  // ID of the configuration to use to extract data from the file, as provided by the `generateExtractionConfig` tool.
  configurationId: string;
  // ID of the file to extract, as returned by the file upload tool or provided by the user
  fileId: string;
  // Project ID that the tool should use. Uses the default project if not provided.
  projectId?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Document processing for agents

Get a pre-signed URL to upload a file to the LlamaParse S3 storage. Not available when authenticating with an API key — use uploadFileByUrl instead. This tool is part of plugin `LlamaParse`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__llamaparse_getuploadurl(args: {
  // Project ID that the tool should use. Uses the default project if not provided.
  projectId?: string;
  // Expected downstream processing workload for the file to upload. Allowed values: 'user_data', 'parse', 'extract', 'split', 'classify', 'sheet', 'agent_app'. Defaults to 'parse' if not provided.
  purpose?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Document processing for agents

Parse a file providing its file ID, retrieving markdown or plain text content of the file. Use with file IDs obtained with the getUploadUrl/uploadFileByUrl tool or that the user provided. This tool is part of plugin `LlamaParse`.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__codex_apps__llamaparse_parsefile(args: {
  // ID of the file to parse, as returned by the file upload tool or provided by the user
  fileId: string;
  // Whether to extract markdown or plain text. Defaults to true (extract markdown).
  markdown?: boolean;
  // Specific pages to limit the parsing operation to
  pages?: Array<number>;
  // Project ID that the tool should use. Uses the default project if not provided.
  projectId?: string;
  // Parsing mode to use. While agentic or agentic_plus are recommended, this parameter defaults to cost_effective if not specified.
  tier?: "cost_effective" | "agentic" | "agentic_plus";
  // API version to use. Defaults to `latest` if not specified.
  version?: "latest" | string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
